{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler stitch task (#5315) to implement `cmd/sha512sum/main.go` - a SHA-512 checksum utility for the go-unix-utils project. The task title is \"[stitch] cmd/sha512sum basic hashing (srd033 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\". The task requires creating a single file that computes SHA-512 digests of files/stdin and outputs them in GNU format, following the exact same pattern as the existing `cmd/sha256sum/main.go`. Git is managed externally by the orchestrator - no git commands should be run.\n\n   Task requirements:\n   - R1: Compute SHA-512 digest of files, output in GNU two-space format\n   - R2: Hash stdin when no file args or \"-\" is given\n   - R3: Support binary mode flag (-b) with asterisk-prefixed filename\n   - R4: Install SIGPIPE handler, support --version and --help flags\n\n   Design decisions:\n   - D1: Use `pkg/hashutil.HashConfig` with `crypto/sha512.New` and `DigestLen 64`\n   - D2: Delegate file iteration and formatting to `pkg/hashutil.DigestFiles`\n   - D3: Follow the exact same `main()` structure as `cmd/sha256sum`\n\n   Acceptance criteria:\n   - AC1: `go build -o bin/sha512sum ./cmd/sha512sum/` compiles without errors\n   - AC2: `echo hello | bin/sha512sum` outputs correct SHA-512 digest with `-` as filename\n   - AC3: `bin/sha512sum file.txt` outputs correct digest with filename\n   - AC4: `bin/sha512sum -b file.txt` outputs asterisk-prefixed filename\n   - AC5: `bin/sha512sum --version` prints version info and exits 0\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - SHA-512 hashing using Go's `crypto/sha512` standard library\n   - GNU checksum format: `HASH  FILENAME` (text) or `HASH *FILENAME` (binary)\n   - BSD tag format: `SHA512 (FILENAME) = HASH`\n   - Shared `pkg/hashutil` package for checksum protocol (HashConfig, DigestFiles, FormatGNU, etc.)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing against `gsha512sum` (Homebrew GNU coreutils)\n   - Checksum verification mode (`--check`)\n   - NUL-delimited output (`--zero`)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `cmd/sha256sum/main.go` (READ - reference implementation to follow exactly)\n     - This is the template for sha512sum. It shows the exact structure: SIGPIPE handler, flag parsing, HashConfig construction, DigestFiles/VerifyChecksums delegation\n     - Key structure: `main()` calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`, parses args, builds `hashutil.HashConfig{Algorithm: \"SHA256\", NewHash: sha256.New, DigestLen: 32}`, handles `--check` mode vs digest mode\n     - Full code (172 lines) includes: helpText/versionText constants, main(), nulWriter struct, options struct, parseArgs(), parseLongFlag(), parseShortFlags()\n     ```go\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         cfg := hashutil.HashConfig{\n             Algorithm: \"SHA256\",\n             NewHash:   sha256.New,\n             DigestLen: 32,\n         }\n         // ... check mode or digest mode\n         os.Exit(hashutil.DigestFiles(files, cfg, opts.binary, opts.tag, stdout, os.Stderr))\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd033-sha512sum.yaml` (READ - full SRD)\n     - Defines all requirements R1-R4, goals G1-G3, non-goals, and acceptance criteria\n     - Package contract imports: `pkg/hashutil` and `pkg/sys`\n\n   - `pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go` (READ - shared hash infrastructure)\n     - Defines `HashConfig` struct: `{Algorithm string, NewHash func() hash.Hash, DigestLen int}`\n     - Defines `CheckOptions` struct: `{Warn bool, Quiet bool, Status bool}`\n     - Exports: `FormatGNU()`, `FormatBSDTag()`, `ComputeDigest()`\n\n   - `pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go` (provided inline in prompt)\n     - Ex